# Array bidirectional growth and drain performance

Measures 1,000,000 iterations that push one value after the last element and
one value before the first element, which grows one contiguous allocation in
both directions, and then drains the resulting 2,000,000 elements from both
ends. The workload measures the bidirectional growth policy together with both
removal paths, and the printed removal count proves every element was produced
exactly once.

>>> source
let values: int[] = []
for (iteration in 0..1000000) {
    values->push(iteration)
    values->unshift(iteration)
}
let removed: int = 0
while (values->shift() != null) {
    removed = removed + 1
}
while (values->pop() != null) {
    removed = removed + 1
}
print(removed)
